<title>NORWAY: Saga's Tordis due back onstream after maintenance.</title>
<headline>Saga's Tordis due back onstream after maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil production at the North Sea Tordis oilfield was due to resume on Wednesday following a five-day stoppage for scheduled maintenance, operator Saga Petroleum ASA said.</p>
<p>&quot;We shut down on Friday for planned maintenance and we will be back in production later today,&quot; Saga spokesman Bjoern Schibevaag said.</p>
<p>The 75,000 barrel per day development feeds crude to the Gullfaks C platform for processing and loading on to shuttle tankers.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
